Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-23
Subject: Drop virtual from TList.Error for the bootstrap subset
License: expat

The FPC 2.0.2 compiler sources declare `TList.Error` as a virtual
class procedure.  The tp2cc bootstrap only implements the non-virtual
static subset of Pascal class methods, and this compiler tree does not
need virtual dispatch for `TList.Error`.

Make that one declaration honest for the subset we actually bootstrap:
keep it as a class procedure, but stop claiming virtual dispatch.

--- a/compiler/cclasses.pas
+++ b/compiler/cclasses.pas
@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@
      function Add(Item: Pointer): Integer;
      procedure Clear; dynamic;
      procedure Delete(Index: Integer);
-     class procedure Error(const Msg: string; Data: Integer); virtual;
+     class procedure Error(const Msg: string; Data: Integer);
      procedure Exchange(Index1, Index2: Integer);
      function Expand: TList;
      function Extract(item: Pointer): Pointer;
